---

A built-in language primitive with special evaluation rules that cannot be implemented as a regular function (e.g., `if`, `lambda`, `define` in Lisp). In other words, special forms are necessary for cases where ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/derived-form.td")}s do not suffice.
